From: iDeck local development <ideck-local@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Mark iOS QEMU cross executables as requiring a wrapper

Class: build-fix

Evidence: experiments/linux-guest/evidence/qemu-cross-build.json; Apple execution pending

Applied only to the locked QEMU source staged by the iOS Linux Probe recipe.
Meson's Darwin/arm64 host heuristic cannot distinguish iOS from macOS. Keep
the real compiler and machine settings, but do not try to execute iOS programs
on the macOS build host. Native configure invocations remain unchanged.

Offered-upstream: no, local experiment
---
diff --git a/configure b/configure
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -1843,6 +1843,10 @@ if test "$skip_meson" = no; then
 
   echo "# Automatically generated by configure - do not modify" > $cross
   echo "[properties]" >> $cross
+  # This iOS recipe's Darwin/arm64 device binaries cannot execute on macOS.
+  if test "$cross_compile" = "yes"; then
+    echo "needs_exe_wrapper = true" >> $cross
+  fi
 
   # unroll any custom device configs
   for a in $device_archs; do
